    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a much better direction. You're starting to grasp the essence of it—it's about the cost of resistance, not just the legality of the claim. It's reminiscent of the lessons I had to instill in the fleet back then; if the threat of retaliation is seen as a mere calculation rather than a terrifying certainty, you've already lost the initiative.\n\nIf I were to use that \"asymmetric\" approach to secure a specific maritime corridor, how would you suggest masking the true intent of the buildup? We used to rely on seasonal movements and atmosphere to hide our preparations, but today, everything is watched by satellites. How can a leader maintain that sense of overwhelming, inevitable presence while keeping the \"unification\" you mentioned from forming?",
